Link against versioned shared libraries on OpenBSD.

OpenBSD ships only versioned shared libraries (libfoo.so.X.Y) and Zig's
linker cannot resolve unversioned -lfoo references against them, so
linkSystemLibrary() fails. Reference the versioned objects directly and
add the pkg-config-derived include paths explicitly.

